# DHI-11 V5 — Orris/Tonkarome scientific-data audit — 2026-09-05

**Implemented at fixed doses. Current diagnostic: 106 PASS / 36 WARN / 3 FAIL / 1 SKIP; diagnostic overall FAIL; controlling release decision HOLD.** All 23 stock bindings remain PASS. G15 is PASS and the planned-volume receipt is BOUND, with physical-metrology and release authority false. The six architecture declarations still match; that is not a match to Dior's confidential ingredient formula.

The 30 mL and half-size pour schedules are unchanged. Irotyl remains excluded by the design constraint; this audit does not purport to prove the undisclosed commercial formula's complete composition.

## Primary evidence and claim boundaries

### Orris Liquid

[PerfumersWorld SKU 8IQ24653](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=8IQ24653) gives an 80–85% irone description but no fraction basis, isomer distribution or owned-lot assay. Its specific gravity is not a verified 25 °C working-stock density. The [linked documents](https://www.perfumersworld.com/document-list.php?pro_id=8IQ24653) lack an IFRA certificate and usable composition/physical-property data; the displayed generic CoA is not an irone assay or a match to the owned lot.

**Adjudication:** the former 0.825 alpha-irone-equivalent constituent tuple is withdrawn. Coverage zero means no accepted assay, not zero irones. The confirmed preparation is 9% w/w supplied product in DEP, not 9% pure irone. Product OAV remains UNKNOWN; the system must not fall through to a numerical monomolecular OAV.

[Yamazaki and Miyazaki's 2025 study](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-08925-z) compares specific orris/irone samples and reports character differences and impurity effects. It supports caution about alpha-irone equivalence; it is not an assay of SKU 8IQ24653, a product ODT measurement, proof of DHI2011 ingredients, or a finished-perfume optimum. No numerical liking ratio was extracted.

### Tonkarome

[PW SKU 2QV23715](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=2QV23715) identifies a mixture and tonka substitute associated with Synarome. The [Ventós specification](https://ventos.com/index.php/?codi=001_RAYOWSKUET_3969&idi=EN&option=com_evsa&task=documentacion.mostrar) identifies coumarin, reports vapor pressure undetermined and supplies no density. The inventory's Firmenich attribution is unresolved, not silently rewritten as a different physical bottle.

The [PW public documents](https://www.perfumersworld.com/document-list.php?pro_id=2QV23715) are internally inconsistent: SDS benzyl benzoate 40–50% and coumarin 20–30% do not reconcile with the allergen table's benzyl benzoate 7.2366% and missing coumarin row. Category 4 maxima differ by listed application; a conformity statement coexists with a prohibited-material notice. The generic CoA appearance also differs from the product description. These are disputed supplier assertions, not accepted composition or safety clearance.

**Adjudication:** classify Tonkarome as an opaque mixture. MW 160, VP 0.05 Pa and the two ODT estimates have no verified product measurement here. Keep legacy numbers visibly labeled as placeholders for diagnostic continuity, but withhold its OAV. Coumarin presence does not establish glycoside precursors or their transformation on skin. Preserve the 20% w/w supplied-product preparation in TEC.

[IFRA's official guidance](https://ifrafragrance.org/initiatives-positions/safe-use-fragrance-science/ifra-standards) states that conformity documentation does not replace a safety assessment. Missing or conflicting documentation cannot be repaired by choosing a generous application limit.

## Implemented corrections

| Failure mechanism | Corrected behavior |
|---|---|
| Catalog midpoint promoted to Orris constituent composition | Remove the invented tuple; retain explicit hold metadata, sources and limitations |
| Tonkarome treated as a single molecule | Opaque-mixture classification; OAV and intensity UNKNOWN during initial and time/amount-evolved states |
| Unknown mixture data contributing ordinary estimated confidence | Quarantined-source labels receive the maximum unavailable-evidence flag, not an ordinary estimate; not a statistical uncertainty interval |
| Tonkarome substring matched natural tonka glycosides | Explicit evidence-needed warning replaces the asserted transformation |
| Wrong concentration-basis attribute; duplicate carrier warning | Read declared stock_fraction_basis; reject unsupported/undeclared bases once per material |
| Four catalog-density projections called authoritative grams | Keep projected active_g as diagnostic only; withhold authoritative mass without lot/temperature evidence |
| Missing IFRA limit called compliant | Explicit incomplete coverage; absent limits do not mean unrestricted |
| Exact/profile limit lookup discarded zero | Preserve zero, reject any positive amount under a zero limit, avoid division by zero and JSON infinity |
| Scorer/gate alias coverage disagreement | Gate includes every unchecked scorer identity; do not silently resolve conflicting AIMI limits |
| Volume-based safety screen claiming mass-based authorization | Always provisional; even an independent mass chain does not mean this volume scorer evaluated it |
| UNKNOWN OAV rendered as absent family contribution | Report known-subset percentages with incomplete full-mixture scope; all-unknown families display UNKNOWN |
| Scientific analysis displayed after gate labels | Full formatter now leads with headspace and temporal evidence; explicit UTF-8/Unicode output supported |

Orris stock metadata now mirrors 9% w/w DEP. Tonkarome's case-colliding catalog/runtime rows were consolidated into one record with the original supplier SKU, the confirmed 20% w/w TEC preparation and qualified provenance. Legacy numerical fields are not newly validated. The ignored material-properties cache has corrected Orris stock wording/fraction and explicit proxy warnings; no global generator rewrite was run. That cache remains a legacy consumer and must not supply release or hedonic authority.

No inventory.txt bytes, authority overlay pins, historical stock receipts, unrelated stock records, formula doses or parent V4 bytes were changed in this audit. No new pipeline script, physical bottle event, external-provider call, commit or push was made.

## Diagnostic changes and what they mean

| Gate | Previous stock-reconciled run | Current scientific audit |
