| master_perfumer_gate | PASS | WARN |
| concentration_basis | WARN | PASS |

The three failures are two material-evidence gaps plus their aggregate, not three demonstrated smell defects. Recognizing a proprietary blend does not itself mean that the blend smells bad. No opacity allowance was enabled to clear this run.

The remaining 36 warnings include genuine safety/mass/carrier and data-quality gaps, plus legacy receptor caps, generic family/OAV targets, price assumptions and aesthetic heuristics. Those heuristic warnings were not promoted to scientific laws or used to alter the perfume. The original six intended helper roles that screened low remain hypotheses for controlled omission tests, not proof of dispensability. Numerical balances now exclude two unknown OAVs and cannot decide whether the perfume is iris-led.

## Mass and safety evidence still required

All 23 delivered masses remain unmeasured and all 23 authoritative-active-mass fields are unavailable. Seventeen rows use density fallbacks. The four working-stock fractions are known, but fraction alone does not establish delivered product mass or carrier volume. The four formerly exact natural masses were catalog-density projections, not weighed exceptions.

Thirteen current-formula names lack explicit local Category 4 records. This count is not a regulatory blacklist. AIMI additionally has conflicting alternate-name entries; neither 7.26 nor 20.0 is automatically accepted. The worksheet enumerates every row and the needed document/measurement.

The [mass and safety worksheet](../../formulas/DHI-11_V5_MASS_AND_SAFETY_WORKSHEET.md) supplies blank lot-bound records, carrier equations, raw-stock-concentrate and finished-batch denominator definitions, and the existing measurement-workflow boundary. Delivered-mass fields in the design JSON are placeholders, not release-CLI inputs. A reviewed ingestion bridge and real evidence remain necessary; the audit did not fabricate either.

## What the system has and has not learned

Persisted knowledge consists of corrected source interpretation, withdrawal rules, alias/zero-limit/unknown-value negative controls and a traceable evidence checklist. This is testable project behavior, not new sensory data or a model-weight update.

The formula is still NOT COMPOUNDED. Liking, DHI2011 similarity, smoothness, layer distinctness, diffusion, longevity and stability remain NOT TESTED. Research and unit tests cannot establish absolute hedonism. After safety and execution requirements are satisfied, the next sensory evidence is the existing blinded, carrier-matched comparison/omission protocol with repeated observations—not a higher ingredient count or an optimized OAV score.

## Verification

The initial 20-case negative-control suite reproduced 16 failures and had 4 existing passes. One early post-fix test selected a sorted row by position instead of name; that test bug was corrected. Independent native read-only reviews found the alias-coverage, tiny zero-limit, unknown-family and source-confidence issues; the parent verified and fixed them.

The final affected-consumer run passed **264 tests, 0 failures across 12 files**. Its **7,360 warnings** are repeated instances of the same pytest_asyncio deprecation under Python 3.14, not 7,360 perfume warnings. Stale stock/coverage expectations were replaced with current explicit identities and arithmetic coverage checks; no evidence-coverage score floor was lowered to retain a false pass. A full repository/release suite was not run.

