Literature-first and verification skills kept edits source-led and scoped; native reviewers were read-only and the parent retained scientific decisions, edits and verification. Plugin Management exposed management operations rather than a literature-search facility, so no plugin permission or installation was changed. Research used built-in primary-source browsing.

## DHP reference preference — 2026-09-06

The user explicitly selected **DHP 2025 — newer reference** for related Dior comparison. The selected local key is `iris_sandalwood.dhp2025`, with qualitative secondary-reference use only: its numerical ingredient requirements and OAV ratios are not accepted without revalidation. DHI 2011 remains the formula target and current diagnostic archetype. No dose, physical stock, Irotyl exclusion, safety boundary or acceptance threshold was changed for this preference.

The repository contains two different design heuristics in `engine/families/registry.py`: `leather_iris_amber.dhp2014`, with leather/oud anchors, and `iris_sandalwood.dhp2025`, with Sandalore/Polysantol anchors and Irotyl among allowed iris-group members. These are local assumptions, not authenticated Dior formulas, measured reference profiles or verified ingredient lists. They must not automatically supply replacement materials or numerical acceptance criteria for DHI 2011.

The current [official Dior Homme Parfum description](https://www.dior.com/en_int/beauty/products/dior-homme-parfum-E000000226.html), checked on September 6, attributes the reinterpretation to Francis Kurkdjian and describes root-to-flower iris alongside an amber accord featuring patchouli, vetiver and coumarin notes. This supports a broad reference discussion; it does not establish the registry's named sandalwood molecules, their minimum ratios, an Irotyl ingredient claim, or a DHI 2011 composition. The older DHP version was not authenticated from this current page. No DHP-specific diagnostic has been run or accepted.

The selected comparison is now explicit: (1) use the iris root/powder relationship to question V5's proposed Orris/irone/ionone structure, without claiming it matches DHP; (2) compare the intended warm interior with the described amber/coumarin direction, while Tonkarome composition remains unresolved; (3) recognize the deliberate wood difference—V5 has a cedar/vetiver return and no selected patchouli stock. That difference is not automatically a defect because DHI 2011 remains the target. No Sandalore, Polysantol, patchouli or Irotyl is added to satisfy the adjacent reference model. This is a source-led structural comparison, not a newly passed computational or sensory test.

Final artifact checks found that a new current-status paragraph placed in the formula definition changed its semantic hash despite unchanged dose rows. The paragraph was moved into the existing Pipeline Analysis section rather than changing the report binding or formula definition. The fixed-dose master retains semantic SHA-256 `279ba9f447847b63313b151bb0d5b059b10c160305947d514739ba3617c27232`; the raw report remains immutable. The independent pour card and this audit retain current status prominently.
